#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084455 :tutorial/content "We have learned how to solve quadratic equations by factoring. Just like quadratic equations, some (but not all) cubic equations can also be solved by factoring.\n\nTo solve a cubic equation by factoring, we just need to follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Write the equation with $0$ on one side\n\n2\\. Factor the expression on the other side\n\n3\\. Set each factor equal to $0$ and solve\n\nTo factor the cubic, we can often use the method of grouping.\n\n**Note:** The cubic equations in the following examples can all be factored, but keep in mind that most cubic equations cannot be!" :tutorial/id #uuid "3c5846e9-07ca-5d29-824a-9bb84c33473a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3710 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
